# =============================================================================
# BENCHMARK REGISTRY AUTHORITY (BR-2) — GOVERNED SURFACE
# =============================================================================
#
# Ratified 2026-08-20 (ADR §35 D-20). BR-2B's safety property is capability
# absence, not the absence of every conceivable private callable. The latter is
# not provable in Python — closures, containers, dynamic attributes, exec and
# runtime rebinding put it out of reach — and three audits found seven bypasses
# on exactly that seam before the claim was withdrawn.
#
# Private-source expansion is therefore governed here rather than gated in CI.
# A contributor who can modify production code AND its tests in one commit is
# stopped by an independent approving review, not by a generated artifact they
# can regenerate in the same commit.
#
# CODEOWNERS IS NOT ENFORCEMENT. It routes review requests and nothing more.
# It becomes a control only with branch protection configured per
# docs/governance/PROTECTED_BRANCHES.md: require a pull request, require review
# from Code Owners, require at least one approval from someone other than the
# author, and dismiss stale approvals on push. Without those settings every line
# below is advisory.
#
# INDEPENDENCE IS AN OPEN OWNER DECISION. The owner named below is also the
# author of this work. A single owner reviewing their own change is not an
# independent review, whatever branch protection is configured. Substituting a
# distinct reviewer or team here is the step that makes this a real control.

# The shipped package: production source, its manifests, and its pinned digests.
